# Guards and validation run on in-process rpc calls during server rendering
# (docs/design/28-rpc-wire-format.md): the Report page's @Load calls its
# protocol in-process, as a guest, then as a user, then as an admin. The
# script is one browser; its session cookie follows it.

### a guest's in-process calls are refused by the guards, and validated
GET /report
>>> 200
~ report: secret: rejected unauthenticated; admin: rejected unauthenticated; blank: invalid credentials.name: Enter your name; named: checked ada

### sign in without a role
POST /inproc.vault.VaultProtocol/SignIn
content-type: application/json
connect-protocol-version: 1
origin: http://localhost

{"name": "ada", "admin": false}
>>> 200

### Authenticated passes; Role(.admin) is forbidden
GET /report
>>> 200
~ report: secret: the vault; admin: rejected forbidden; blank: invalid credentials.name: Enter your name; named: checked ada

### sign in as an admin
POST /inproc.vault.VaultProtocol/SignIn
content-type: application/json
connect-protocol-version: 1
origin: http://localhost

{"name": "root", "admin": true}
>>> 200

### every guard passes
GET /report
>>> 200
~ report: secret: the vault; admin: the admin vault; blank: invalid credentials.name: Enter your name; named: checked ada

### a rate limit counts in-process calls: two are allowed
GET /limited
>>> 200
~ limited: allowed

### the second
GET /limited
>>> 200
~ limited: allowed

### and the third is refused
GET /limited
>>> 200
~ limited: rejected rate limited true
